# API Endpoint Rules

## Purpose
Defines mandatory API design standards: enforce RESTfulness, predictable and reusable endpoints, strict pagination/filtering/sorting. All deviations are invalid.

---

## Endpoint Structure
- Base: `/api/v<version>/<module>/...` (initial release: `v1`)
- All module endpoints must have `/api/v<version>/` prefix
- CRUD:
  - `GET /<resource>`: list
  - `GET /<resource>/:id`: get one
  - `POST /<resource>`: create
  - `PUT /<resource>/:id`: update
  - `DELETE /<resource>/:id`: soft-delete
- Nested: `/<resource>/:id/<subresource>`

### System Endpoints (Not under `/api/v<version>`)
- System: `GET /health`, `/ready`, `/live` (never under `/api/v<version>`; see `health-checks.mdc`)

---

## Query Parameters
- Pagination: `page` (default 1), `limit` (per module default)
- Filtering: snake_case queries (ex: `/users?status=active&role=admin`)
- Sorting: `sort_by=<field>&order=asc|desc`; default order required per resource

---

## Request & Response
- Validate requests via Zod (`@validations/*`)
- No business logic in routes
- Must use standard response format (`response-format.mdc`)
- Errors handled via central middleware
- Lists (`GET /<resource>`): must paginate using `@lib/response` pagination helpers (use DEFAULT_PAGE, DEFAULT_PAGE_LIMIT, MAX_PAGE_LIMIT from `@config/constants`); always return pagination metadata

---

## Middleware Order
1. Validation (Zod)
2. Auth (JWT)
3. RBAC
4. Handler (`@lib/async/asyncHandler`)
- All handlers must use `asyncHandler`

---

## HTTP Methods & Status
- `GET`: 200
- `POST`: 201
- `PUT`/`PATCH`: 200
- `DELETE`: 204 (see `response-format.mdc` for exceptions)
- Client: 400, 401, 403, 404; Server: 500

---

## Versioning & URLs
- `/api/v<version>/...` required (initial release: `/api/v1/...`)
- No breaking changes without version bump
- Must be backward compatible

---

## Multiplatform Support
- Must be client-agnostic (Web, Android, iOS, Desktop)
- Detection: `User-Agent` (analytics) or `X-Platform` (optional)
- Platform optimizations must be transparent (e.g., compression, pagination cap)
- Response format and API version same for all platforms; feature flags for platform-specific features
- CORS per `cors.mdc`; Auth per `auth-security.mdc` (JWT) must be consistent

---

## Forbidden
- Mixing GET/POST semantics
- Returning raw DB objects
- Hardcoded pagination/filters
- Business logic in routes
- Platform-specific versions or responses
- Undocumented/Non-REST verbs (except allowed `POST /<resource>/:id/<action>` in `dev-plan/P010_api_endpoints.mdc` with validation & auth)

---

## Enforcement
❌ Any violation is invalid  
✅ Strict compliance required; refactors must improve consistency, usability, and maintainability
